
== nsh 0.4.0 (e626a8d)

== Generate throwaway keys (kept out of git under .nsh/keys)
root key exists; keys are never overwritten
release key exists; keys are never overwritten

== Certify the release key for this app family, 90 days
$ nsh certify --root .nsh/keys/root.secret --key .nsh/keys/release.pub --apps com.example.nshstarter.* --days 90 -o .nsh/keys/release.cert
.nsh/keys/release.cert: key 3ba2d79a65cea38d certified by root a4317b851e3a8d7e for com.example.nshstarter.* until 90 days from now

== Publish the package (signed with the release key)
$ nsh publish App.tsx --key .nsh/keys/release.secret --cert .nsh/keys/release.cert -o .nsh/out/com.example.nshstarter.remote-1.nshpkg
warn app id `com.example.nshstarter.remote` is a placeholder: give the app an id under a domain you own before releasing it, as apps with one id share their data
